.DS_Store
benchmark_profiles/*
notes
flm.sh
docs/gw.md

# Generated coverage artifacts (AUD-049): regenerated on demand by
# `make test-coverage-focused` / `make coverage-report`; never a source of truth,
# so it must not be tracked (a committed copy only drifts stale — it was last
# regenerated at M21 while the code moved on).
coverage-focused.txt
coverage-focused.tmp.txt
coverage-focused.html

# Formal-verification run artifacts (AUD-046): the pinned tools jar is fetched
# on demand (SHA-256-verified) and the state-count summary is regenerated each
# run by scripts/formal/run_tlc.sh — neither is a source of truth to track.
.tlacache/
tlc-summary.txt

# Compiled example binaries
api_workflow
comprehensive
dag_patterns
error_handling
integration_check
new_simple
# observability example: ignore the compiled binary only, not the dir (anchored
# path so the pattern can't swallow the examples/observability/ source tree).
/examples/observability/observability

# Generated runtime state written by the api_workflow example when run (not source).
/examples/api_workflow/api_workflow_state/

# Anvil agent-team harness (M5/Phase 15 REL-02): never commit harness state into
# the library tree. These are tracked-or-untracked working artifacts of the
# multi-agent workflow, not part of the published module. Excluding them here
# stops a future `git add -A` from sweeping the harness into a release commit.
.planning/
.smtc/
.smtc-cache/
anvil
anvil-up
spawn/
ANVIL-TEAM.md
.mcp.json

# Local experiment sandbox (not part of the library)
playground/
.claude/

# TLC model-checker scratch output (timestamped run dirs under specs/)
specs/states/

# Doc-sample gate temp build dirs (internal/doctest buildAndRun)
.doctest*

# Local dogfood harness (dev-only, never shipped)
_local/

# Runtime store artifacts produced by RUNNING an example or a probe. JSONFileStore's
# baseDir is a DIRECTORY named for the path the caller passes, so `go run
# ./examples/new_simple` creates ./workflow_data.json/ next to the module root and fills
# it with live run state — a __timestamp, node statuses, outputs.
#
# It was committed once (2fea479) by a `git add -A`, which is exactly why that command is
# the wrong instrument in a shared tree. Ignored here rather than only deleted, because
# deleting it fixes today and ignoring it fixes every future example run.
workflow_data.json/
*_workflow_data/
audit/*